  "notes": "UniAD 1.0 base (uniad_base_e2e.pth, trained on nuScenes, zero-shot here) on all 220 Bench2Drive routes, 9-12 Nov 2026, at fastcode-shakaal (one RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell, shared with other users' jobs), six lanes (sites b2duv-lane0..5-fastcode-shakaal). Paddock eval/uv: PR #167's Bench2Drive code (patch 0003, /observe) with the uniad/vad adapters of models/uniad-vad. Bench2Drive 7ec25d1 + patches 0001-0003. 2 Hz (planning_hz), waypoint_dt 0.5, paddock's six-camera rig, no early stop (Bench2Drive's own end conditions, as the Drive-JEPA, Qwen-Drive and VisionPilot 220-route records), up to three attempts a route: an attempt the leaderboard ended as a simulation or agent crash was set aside and the route driven again. Under GPU contention the node ran at 0.009-0.05x real time; per_route_timeout_s was raised from 5400 to 10800 s (wall clock only), and route 2084 finished past it while only the harness process was paused (the evaluator, CARLA and node kept driving). 220 of 220 source runs kept no run.json, so their routes are attributed to uniad on the tree they were found in; config.model_env and the rest of config are what 220/220 source runs recorded. asked for a plan at 2 Hz, the planning_hz the model's model.yaml declared for these runs, the last plan followed in between.",
